148 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (In modern buildings, lift systems are essential for efficient transportation across floors. However, conventional lift systems often operate on basic pre-programmed logic, leading to inefficiencies such as prolonged wait times, unnecessary stops, and high energy consumption. This project aims to develop a smart lift system using machine learning techniques to optimize lift operations. By predicting future lift calls based on historical usage patterns and current conditions, the system will improve the overall efficiency, reducing wait times and energy consumption. The model will be trained on synthesized time-series data to anticipate user demands and optimize lift movement.)
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
